Right, yeah. Where the G.I.

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.960
Joe has to fight the original giant Cobra.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.420
Well, the prequel was G.I.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:38.760
Joseph. Right.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.280
All right, so back to the team management for a second.

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:48.280
Other than the characters feeling different, is there, like, is there some strategy behind this, too?

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:52.920
Is there any planning to, like, all right, like, this guy's got these strengths and weaknesses,

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:57.080
so I'm going to save them for these stages, or I don't want to lose this team member here,

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.300
so I'm not going to use them?

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:02.580
Or is it just kind of, like, pick your favorites and just keep going with them until they die?

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:12.700
Well, I think it's not so much that, I guess if any level is sort of designed for any specific character,

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:16.200
it's probably going to be the one that you're forced to take with you,

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:22.020
and that's sort of, as the game goes on, you sort of rotate through who the forced character is,

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:23.560
and you get to add whoever else.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:30.360
But beyond that, I'd say that the, like, where the strategy actually comes in isn't really,

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.480
it's not specific to any particular character.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:39.480
It's just making sure that you're, like, balancing them properly.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:43.760
And that's more, that's not even just, like, oh, I've got to make sure to take this guy out,

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:47.220
just to make sure he, like, levels up, too.

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:57.500
But that's also, like, just in each level, you've got to rotate out just so that you're kind of spreading the pain a bit,

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.520
so that you don't have, you're not just, like, killing them all.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:08.380
Between each, like, sub-stage, your health stays the same.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:14.040
So you could get to the end and have your first guy almost dead,

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:18.020
and you don't want him to die, so you've got to switch to somebody else.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:24.500
If you guys remember Thunderbirds on the NES, which was also a licensed video game,

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:29.660
that was the one that, it had, like, the 60 in-game days to defeat the hood.

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:30.820
Yes. But...

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:31.920
And they were the marionettes.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.280
Right, right, with the marionettes.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:39.600
But, like, it had you rotate between the team members and their vehicles, but not at your own.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.520
Like, you couldn't choose who to pick.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:42.740
It just made the missions.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:51.300
This feels like maybe what we wanted, where it's like you can pick the play style that best suits the way that you go through the game.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:56.400
Like, as you continue to, whether you beat the game or not, like, as you continue to keep playing it,

00:20:56.560 --> 00:21:02.820
you get good with certain characters or learn how to, you know, do better on certain stages with certain characters.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:08.880
You can have it be the loadout that you want, but the missions remain the same rather than the way Thunderbirds laid it out.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.420
Yeah, I think anything...

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.120
Yeah, I think that gives it more replay value.

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:20.580
Yeah. I think that anything that sort of gives you any kind of meaningful choice is better than not that.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:27.360
And I think being able to select who you take with you is a way to empower.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.940
So I appreciated that.

00:21:28.940 --> 00:21:31.660
The way the game starts is a little strange.

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.720
If you don't know anything about G.I.

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:39.240
Joe like me, it's just a guy who obviously turns out to be General Hawk.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:45.760
But it's just a guy shows up on a giant TV and says, well, it's time to get rid of the Cobra organization.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.620
That doesn't sound like...

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.920
What's the date today? Yeah, it's time.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.220
It's like, that doesn't sound like how this works.

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:58.960
Shouldn't we be told that they bombed a school or something and that we have to now get revenge on them?

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:02.280
That seems like too much of a bummer, Mike.

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:05.460
Nobody wants to do anything after hearing about that.

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.480
We sound like the terrorist organization.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.320
Well, because what you're describing, it's come full circle.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:13.920
This is how I played action figures.

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:18.720
Me and my friend, we'd play with our action figures and I would just be like, all right, I'm going to head over to the bad guys base.

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:20.320
Yeah. Like, fight the bad guys.

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:21.560
Like, that's like literally what we would do.

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:23.340
It's like, yeah, that's what we do. We fight the bad guys.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:25.180
There's no reason that they're bad guys.

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:27.540
We're good guys. They're just the bad guys and we're just the good guys.

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.600
And we're just going to go over and fight the bad guys now.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:33.560
It would just be like, it was like I'm going out to grab groceries.

00:22:33.820 --> 00:22:35.560
It was like, yeah, I'm going to head over to the bad guys base for a bit.

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:45.060
I'll be back. Well, what Joe is saying is that we've been trained from a young age to believe that there should be no casus belli.

00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:51.280
Like, it's just the, they're just, you are always in the right to be an aggressor.

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:53.140
If you're the good guy.

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:58.080
Yeah, that's what my eight-year-old self was, exactly what he was saying.

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:05.960
And just like in real life, I refuse to believe that Cobra Commander believes himself to be a bad guy.

00:23:07.020 --> 00:23:10.460
Like, he has in his head some twisted, like, right?

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:12.720
It's not just like, oh, I just wanted to be bad.

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.040
He's got to have a belief system.

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:17.140
Well, doesn't he want to, like, rule the world? Yeah, but why?

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:18.620
What does he believe in?

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:23.320
I just don't think that anybody that wants to rule the world is good.

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:27.580
Oh, yeah, yeah, no. Undoubtedly, by our American upbringing, he's a bad guy.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:33.340
But I'm saying, like, he has to have some kind of moral compass himself.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:35.500
I mean, he doesn't.

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:36.480
I don't think he does.

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:37.560
I get what you're saying.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:39.420
I think that's true with a lot of people.

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:41.820
It's like, they say, like, nobody thinks they're the bad guy.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:44.300
I think that that's mostly true.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:47.320
But I think there are some people that they're not trying to be the bad guy.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:48.780
They just don't care that they're the bad guy.

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:50.140
Like, their goal isn't to be bad.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:51.860
Their goal is to have power.

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:53.280
And if they're like, well, that's bad.

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:54.720
They're like, well, I don't care. It's going to give me power.

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:59.440
I think the simpler explanation is that with a property such as G.I.

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:08.060
Joe, like, maybe Cobra Commander does just want to be the bad guy because that's the simplistic nature of it.

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:09.420
Is he funded by Hasbro?

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:11.260
I think so.

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:17.340
Right. So Cobra Commander, the Cobra organization is being funded by Hasbro to keep the G.I.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.180
Joe brand alive. This is big news.

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:20.220
We should blow this up.

00:24:21.340 --> 00:24:24.360
It's all an inside game, man.

00:24:24.740 --> 00:24:25.760
I believe it.

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:30.820
And if you believe the, like, let's just say that Cobra is threatening the world again.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:33.520
The context wasn't given to us, but surely they are.

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:35.380
It's up to the G.I.

00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:41.500
Joe team to destroy a series of Cobra bases laid out across six different missions all over the globe.

00:24:42.820 --> 00:24:50.600
And, you know, it's told kind of like a cartoon with, you know, little briefings and mission leaders.

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:57.560
And then you can believe that you're, like, doing the episode when you're actually playing the gameplay part of it.

00:24:57.560 --> 00:25:07.700
And the plot builds up towards the capture and then rescue of General Hawk before doing a final assault on Cobra Commander.

00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:11.440
The story, I guess, you know, pretty basic.

00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:12.740
But if you are a G.I.

00:25:12.820 --> 00:25:15.060
Joe fan, it is basically what you're looking for, right?

00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:17.700
It's checking those boxes.

00:25:18.120 --> 00:25:19.060
I really did.

00:25:19.380 --> 00:25:26.080
But what he said, the story is told like I was expecting some kind of, like, literary thing.

00:25:27.080 --> 00:25:28.080
It's not like a cartoon.

00:25:28.180 --> 00:25:29.500
It's a military cartoon.

00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:35.180
Yeah, it's like a Bildungsroman about Cobra Commander.

00:25:35.660 --> 00:25:37.360
Like, no, I get what you mean, though.

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:48.340
Yeah, it does feel like episodes and there is sort of an arc with, like, you know, him being captured and all that.

00:25:48.460 --> 00:25:51.400
And then I think, you know, if you were just playing this the first time,

00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:57.320
it would be a pleasant surprise that you learn that you get to play as him.

00:25:57.320 --> 00:26:01.000
I imagine if you knew who that was before playing the game.

00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:02.260
Because he's cool.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:03.980
He's got, like, jetpack and shit.

00:26:04.180 --> 00:26:07.800
So he's, like, a pretty overpowered character.

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:13.980
Right. I like that trend of just you don't start right away with, like, all the plot at the beginning of a game

00:26:13.980 --> 00:26:16.880
and then just working towards the rescue of somebody.

00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:17.740
You start at the end.

00:26:18.720 --> 00:26:19.740
And then you go.

00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:21.880
No, it's like it's kind of interesting, though.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:22.840
It's memento.

00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:27.100
It has a little bit of a twist and turn through it on a very simple scale.

00:26:27.100 --> 00:26:38.160
And I think it satisfies the fans of the franchise at this point to just tell, like, a very straightforward but satisfying G.I.

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:40.640
Joe story. Faux show.

00:26:40.940 --> 00:26:42.380
But we're not here for story.

00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:43.500
We're here for gameplay.

00:26:43.780 --> 00:26:46.420
We're here for what holds up in 2026.

00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:49.320
And so we've talked about the team management.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:50.540
We've talked about the plot.

00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:52.880
We've talked about how we really don't know much about G.I.

00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:55.180
Joe. But how does it feel to play as these guys?

00:26:55.180 --> 00:26:57.140
Is this a fun game?

00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:03.160
When I was first playing this, I was comparing it a bit to Contra.

00:27:03.820 --> 00:27:07.820
And I think that's a little unfair because Contra is an amazing game.

00:27:08.260 --> 00:27:15.660
And instead, I just thought about, like, if we treat this like any old licensed game, though, it's also, like, the complete opposite.

00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:18.040
It's like you can't just treat all licensed games like garbage.

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:20.720
Like, there's a scale there, too.

00:27:20.720 --> 00:27:34.120
And so I think just the difference in feel between the actual six, not just being stat-based, but the fact that they do feel like different characters, which is obviously just different modifiers.

00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:37.800
But the fact that that exists in this game is a strong compliment.

00:27:37.860 --> 00:27:39.920
But how is the actual level design?

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:43.220
So there's also, like, variety in that.

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:45.320
Like, before I even answer, like, how is it at all?

00:27:45.400 --> 00:27:54.120
Like, there's different kinds of levels that follow sort of a pattern between each world, I guess.

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:59.940
Where you start off with sort of just a pretty standard, like, go to the end of the level.

00:28:00.900 --> 00:28:03.240
And then you get kind of a mini boss.

00:28:04.340 --> 00:28:12.360
Then you get a kind of more open, explore-y level where you have to plant a bunch of bombs.

00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:18.960
And then you get another boss.

00:28:19.180 --> 00:28:23.140
There might be another, like, kind of just more straightforward level in the middle there, too.

00:28:23.340 --> 00:28:36.120
But I like that there's more, like, even within the gameplay that they have, like, they have some variety built into the structure of each level.

00:28:38.020 --> 00:28:41.620
But, yeah, the actual gameplay itself, it feels good.

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:43.420
It's simple, but it feels good.

00:28:43.620 --> 00:28:48.560
Yeah, and I felt that, like, the bosses kind of coming up in between there.

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:53.260
Like, they were, especially early on, there were bosses that were, like, mid-level bosses.

00:28:53.460 --> 00:28:56.320
I felt like it was almost like a boss rush game at the beginning.

00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:58.780
Because it was, and I think in a good way.

00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:05.040
Because it felt like it broke up any possible monotony of, like, level design very nicely.

00:29:05.040 --> 00:29:08.880
Like, right when it would maybe start to get tired of, like, going through.

00:29:08.940 --> 00:29:12.820
I think they, like, just know how brief to make some of these levels.

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:18.060
That, like, I think a lot of NES games fall into this trap of, like, they get their level down.

00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:20.100
Then their level takes, like, 40 minutes to get through.

00:29:20.280 --> 00:29:22.420
And you're like, okay, well, I'm tired of doing this anymore.

00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:26.680
Where this, I think, has, like, enough variety in the levels.

00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:29.840
And it changes up with, like, okay, now you're fighting a boss.

00:29:29.840 --> 00:29:31.160
Or now you're, you know, in a vehicle.

00:29:31.780 --> 00:29:35.540
That, um, that that makes it feel fresh.

00:29:35.980 --> 00:29:39.280
Uh, this is, like, not what we were talking about, I don't think.

00:29:39.400 --> 00:29:40.740
But I, I... Hey, take us there.

00:29:40.740 --> 00:29:46.280
Take us there. All right, but I think that, uh, I agree that the game feels really good to play.

00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:47.380
Now, it doesn't feel like Contra.

00:29:47.500 --> 00:29:51.140
I think Contra is deliberately a faster game.

00:29:51.640 --> 00:30:02.300
Where this feels like, to me, what, what shined or shown to me more in this was, like, the feel of your, your, particularly your weapon.

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.840
Not your punch. But, like, your attacks that are with your weapon.

00:30:04.900 --> 00:30:06.520
That always felt, that always felt good.

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:09.140
And that, uh, coupled with the jump and everything.

00:30:09.280 --> 00:30:13.000
I mean, it just, it, it did not feel NES janky.

00:30:13.080 --> 00:30:14.280
I guess is what I'm trying to get at.

00:30:14.280 --> 00:30:21.440
Yeah, I think between the, like, the fact that you can shoot pretty much in any direction, aside from, like, at an angle.

00:30:21.780 --> 00:30:24.300
But, you know, it's, it's kind of a crapshoot.

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:25.860
What game's gonna let you do that?

00:30:26.180 --> 00:30:34.160
Um, that you can really take advantage of the different kinds of, like, guns that you have between each character.

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:43.520
Um, that, that made, that, with the smoothness and the kind of how controllable the jump is,

00:30:43.520 --> 00:30:45.560
made it feel much more precise.

00:30:45.780 --> 00:30:54.300
A bit, a little bit more methodical, uh, than a lot of the, sort of, action, uh, side-scrollers that we've played.

00:30:55.400 --> 00:31:02.080
And I think a lot of these levels, even though they're, uh, you know, they're, they're, like, mission briefings in the game.

00:31:02.160 --> 00:31:03.520
They really do feel like missions.

00:31:03.680 --> 00:31:07.700
Like, you're, they are changing it up enough where you're getting in unique vehicles.

00:31:07.700 --> 00:31:10.520
You're planting C4s.

00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:12.980
You're fighting giant bosses.

00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:14.800
Like, some of these bosses are massive.

00:31:15.300 --> 00:31:23.800
You're, you're doing enough different things throughout where, like, you don't have to learn new, uh, gameplay techniques or anything.

00:31:23.800 --> 00:31:28.800
But it does feel, um, refreshing each time the mission ends.

00:31:29.060 --> 00:31:33.780
Because then, when you jump into the next mission, it's not, okay, do that, but now in the desert, right?

00:31:33.920 --> 00:31:36.280
It, it, it lays itself out a little differently.

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:41.620
The enemy placement or, or, or number of enemies.

00:31:41.660 --> 00:31:43.800
Like, it's not necessarily overwhelming.

00:31:43.800 --> 00:31:49.000
But it can be a difficult game if, especially if you're learning these characters or learning the game.

00:31:49.000 --> 00:32:04.520
I don't think this is the kind of game that is naturally easy, but is the kind of thing that, like, as you play the game more, uh, the, the, the control of the characters, but also, like, the patterns of the enemies becomes a lot easier to recognize.

00:32:05.220 --> 00:32:08.380
And, uh, and getting through these levels becomes a lot easier, too.

00:32:08.380 --> 00:32:22.040
And so, even if, uh, I, I was dying a lot more frequently in the beginning, or I was, like, man, I'm supposed to take these three guys to the end of the mission, but, uh, the two of them are on low health, and I've just got to rely on this one guy now.

00:32:22.040 --> 00:32:25.180
It's like, well, maybe I was playing a little too aggressively or something like that.

00:32:25.180 --> 00:32:41.240
But I do think that there is a lot, um, a lot to like about the moment to moment in this game, and that any sort of, like, pain points in actual gameplay come from, like, particular things that I wasn't doing well at.

00:32:41.340 --> 00:32:49.320
Like, particular enemies that were just making me take a ton of damage, or, um, particular bosses that I, I couldn't, uh, work out their patterns to.

00:32:49.320 --> 00:32:50.660
What do you guys think?

00:32:50.820 --> 00:32:55.280
Were there, were there other pressure points in the game that made, that made it less enjoyable?

00:32:55.680 --> 00:33:06.320
Uh, the only thing that, like, that really, that really stood out to me, and I think in any other game, this wouldn't bother me as much, but I think because of the perception this game gives you, it bothers me a lot more.

00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:16.280
Is that you have these, these three characters in, in any given level, and they don't share a health bar, you know, you can, you can, like, look and see who's got more health.

00:33:16.460 --> 00:33:18.780
Like, you know, I want to switch to this guy, because that guy's low on health.

00:33:19.440 --> 00:33:29.700
But something about the fact that if you die as one character, you lose that character, fair, but then you go back to the beginning of the level as the other two characters bothered me so much.

00:33:29.800 --> 00:33:35.980
I was like, well, they didn't die, we don't share a health pool, we're all, why are we going back to the beginning of the level, and we don't get the other guy back?

00:33:36.300 --> 00:33:42.920
Like, in any other game, you go back to the beginning of the level, it's because you're getting an extra, you're getting a new life with that guy, and the punishment is going back to the beginning.

00:33:43.180 --> 00:33:45.900
In this game, the punishment is I lost that guy, he's dead.

00:33:46.640 --> 00:33:49.420
Now I'm just two people, why do I got to go back to the beginning of the stage?

00:33:49.600 --> 00:33:55.500
Is he dead, or did they have to bring him to, like, the hospital, which they can only do by going backwards, because they killed everybody?

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:58.860
If he brought him to the hospital, why is he still not okay?

00:33:59.140 --> 00:34:00.920
Well, because he's in triage.

00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:04.620
Yeah, it takes time. Okay, well, there's not a hospital forward?

00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:08.140
There are no hospitals in here.

00:34:08.140 --> 00:34:12.260
No, no, no, a forward hospital is risky, though, because then two more people might die.

00:34:12.800 --> 00:34:14.460
Yeah, but two more people, you gotta go back still.

00:34:14.880 --> 00:34:16.800
Is anyone ever really dead in G.I.

00:34:16.920 --> 00:34:19.620
Joe world? That's where I was gonna go.

00:34:19.720 --> 00:34:25.900
You're raising a great point, though, Joe, it is true, it is true that it stops the momentum of what is otherwise a fun experience.

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:31.280
Yeah, and I feel like I'm already being punished by having died, like, that is the punishment.

00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:33.680
Yeah, maybe they should just all have infinite health.

00:34:34.180 --> 00:34:35.540
Yeah, that's what I was saying.

00:34:35.540 --> 00:34:37.740
Right, maybe you should just get a game genie.

00:34:40.180 --> 00:34:59.600
I guess for me, the stuff that didn't feel great was just sort of the level design itself, like the actual construction of the things you can walk on and walk into felt very random.

00:34:59.600 --> 00:35:07.440
Like, there's a lot of, I guess, hidden areas that are kind of, like, randomly placed.

00:35:08.140 --> 00:35:09.900
Some of them are very obvious.

00:35:11.300 --> 00:35:15.340
But it just, it never, like, when you find a, it never felt like finding a secret.

00:35:15.580 --> 00:35:17.980
It just felt like sort of clipping through the geometry.

00:35:19.580 --> 00:35:22.080
And there might be some power-ups there.

00:35:22.220 --> 00:35:30.480
Like, there was never anything, like, that kind of, like, gave you that, like, dopamine rush of, like, oh, I found this secret.

00:35:30.480 --> 00:35:33.880
It was just, like, oh, I guess this is a place that I can go.

00:35:34.220 --> 00:35:36.300
Like, yeah, sometimes there's, like, vehicles there.

00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:45.280
And, like, but there's also, it just didn't feel very polished in that regard, at least.

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:52.420
Yeah, I agree that, yeah, it did feel like there were a lot of, like, yeah, the secret is this wall is not really a wall.

00:35:52.600 --> 00:35:55.360
It's just, you can just walk right through it and things like that.

00:35:55.360 --> 00:36:00.760
And I think that bothered me in every level except for one of the later ones, the desert level.

00:36:01.140 --> 00:36:12.060
I think it's not the same thing, but I think they took that, they took that game design and they, like, turned it to their advantage where you're on the sand dunes at the end.

00:36:12.180 --> 00:36:25.040
And it's, like, clearly you are on square geometric shapes, but it's covered by a layer of, like, these curvy sand dunes that, like, yeah, you're only walking on, like.

00:36:25.360 --> 00:36:28.460
Yeah, you can bump into a wall and, like, I can see that being a little frustrating.

00:36:28.620 --> 00:36:32.200
It's, like, oh, there's a little wall here, but you can't see it because it's, like, you're on, like, the hill of the sand dune.

00:36:32.480 --> 00:36:37.120
But it feels to me like trudging through sand and you've got to jump when you're going up.

00:36:37.120 --> 00:36:45.380
And, like, it just looks so much more polished than it would if they were square geometric shapes that were visual.

00:36:45.380 --> 00:36:49.720
So, like, I think it, like, does a good job of making it look like a more advanced game than it is.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:51.040
Only in that instance.

00:36:51.040 --> 00:36:52.880
I do think in the rest of it, I agree.

00:36:52.900 --> 00:36:56.200
It's, like, very, um, it's almost like lazy secrets.

00:36:56.700 --> 00:37:03.600
Yeah. And you could chalk some of this up to being, like, how you play with your action figures, too.

00:37:03.720 --> 00:37:06.940
And, you know, things are a little larger than life and stuff.

00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:15.240
But there is some, there is some cartoony stuff going on in terms of, like, how high these characters, like, there's some scaling problems here in the game.

00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:24.160
Of, like, how high characters jump and how everything's laid out and how, in general, just, like, the feel of the characters.

00:37:24.160 --> 00:37:32.380
It does feel more like the way somebody controls them when they're, like, you know, you're holding your hand on the action figure and just moving them, flailing them about.

00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:38.040
It doesn't move quite correctly for my eyes.

00:37:38.140 --> 00:37:41.300
Like, I was a little surprised at how high some of these guys jump.

00:37:41.960 --> 00:37:42.860
And that's fine.

00:37:43.580 --> 00:37:46.180
It's fun. Yeah, that's what I was going to say.

00:37:46.260 --> 00:37:48.720
It's fun. It's not, it doesn't look right.

00:37:48.720 --> 00:37:50.720
But it's, I think it's more fun this way.

00:37:50.900 --> 00:37:59.180
Right. And it's the same thing with, like, the progression paths, too, of, like, the power-ups that you find.

00:37:59.400 --> 00:38:05.480
And, you know, it's not like, it didn't need a whole, like, RPG experience system or something.

00:38:05.480 --> 00:38:19.160
But just picking up the right power-ups to continue to level up your character's weapon is a, you know, a good enough system for the game that it's not trying to, like, overly complicate and introduce too many more systems.

00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:24.500
This game, first and foremost, is just kind of like a side-scrolling shooter.

00:38:25.280 --> 00:38:30.120
And shooter even is subjective, too, because you don't have to use the shooter.

00:38:30.260 --> 00:38:32.320
First off, you can just use your melee weapon.

00:38:32.420 --> 00:38:34.460
But you don't have unlimited ammo either.

00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:37.960
It can certainly feel like you have unlimited ammo if you use it sparingly enough.

00:38:37.960 --> 00:38:43.700
But it is something you can run out of if you're not careful and you would have to resort to melee.

00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:48.140
Yeah, I hope you're not on a boss battle when you have to resort to melee.

00:38:48.480 --> 00:39:00.940
Yeah. I feel like I really disregarded the melee aspect of this unless it was, unless they were, like, enemies that I knew I could handle.

00:39:01.120 --> 00:39:03.300
Otherwise, I was just running gun the whole time.

00:39:03.540 --> 00:39:04.720
You know, it's interesting, though.

00:39:04.720 --> 00:39:12.140
I did notice, because I was trying to, because it was pointed out in the manual that, you know, the switching between shooting and melee,

00:39:12.380 --> 00:39:18.520
that the melee does appear, at least in the beginning when your weapons aren't at max, that it does more damage.

00:39:18.960 --> 00:39:24.160
Yeah. It gets rid of the enemies faster by just clobbering them instead of shooting them.

00:39:24.280 --> 00:39:27.820
And it's like, huh, another thing I don't think is how it works in the real world.

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:32.620
No, you gotta, the first bullets out of any gun are the weakest.

00:39:33.700 --> 00:39:35.540
That's true. Yeah, that is accurate.

00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:38.160
So what is the difficulty, then?

00:39:38.260 --> 00:39:40.280
Is it, is it resource pressure?

00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:43.220
Is it just learning to, like, learning the patterns?

00:39:43.220 --> 00:39:46.760
And so the difficulty comes from having to replay the stages often?

00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:48.480
Is it the health meters?

00:39:48.620 --> 00:39:49.760
Like, are you not getting enough health?

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:51.180
Where does the challenge lie?

00:39:51.920 --> 00:39:54.620
I think it's, it's sort of like a war of attrition.

00:39:54.620 --> 00:39:58.840
Like, I think the moment to moment stuff, it's simple enough, it's easy enough.

00:39:58.840 --> 00:40:06.360
It's just that, again, like, from sub, sub level to sub level, like, yes, there are healing items.

00:40:06.360 --> 00:40:16.480
But unless you pick those up and, like, very strategically switch between characters to give them to who needs it most,

00:40:18.780 --> 00:40:29.100
over, over the course of a mission, you can run, you can get very low on health and going into a final boss with everybody on low on health, it can be an issue.

00:40:29.100 --> 00:40:39.820
So I'd say it's more like, it's more a marathon than it is a sprint, and you just have to be mindful of those things.

00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:44.780
Yeah, moment to moment gameplay, I put this at, like, middle of the road NES difficulty.

00:40:44.780 --> 00:40:48.700
It's not one of the easier games, but it's not, like, a crazy challenging game.

00:40:48.740 --> 00:40:56.540
But I do think it compounds on itself as you're going because you're losing, you know, you're losing resources, you're losing allies,

00:40:56.540 --> 00:41:03.080
and then you get to the end and you're like, I did find myself towards the end to kind of go back to your earlier point, Sean.

00:41:03.680 --> 00:41:10.000
By the end of my time playing this, I was like, oh, maybe I should be using melee a little more often when I can afford it.

00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:14.800
So I save my ammo for the bosses later because I was playing like you for the most of the time.

00:41:14.880 --> 00:41:17.040
And then I started, it started to bite me towards the end.

00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:22.700
Yeah. And I never, I didn't get too much further after that to, like, see how much of a difference it would have made.

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:26.300
But I did kind of start to think, oh, maybe I should try this strategy.

00:41:26.540 --> 00:41:35.500
